AWS MULTI-ACCOUNT STORAGE AUDIT -- IAM POLICIES AND DIRECT LAMBDA DEPLOYMENT
================================================================================
1) TARGET ACCOUNT: Create IAM role CentralStorageAuditReadRole in EACH target account.
Trust policy (replace MANAGEMENT_ACCOUNT_ID and EXTERNAL_ID; remove ExternalId condition if not using it):
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [{
    "Effect": "Allow",
    "Principal": {"AWS": "arn:aws:iam::MANAGEMENT_ACCOUNT_ID:role/CentralStorageAuditLambdaRole"},
    "Action": "sts:AssumeRole",
    "Condition": {"StringEquals": {"sts:ExternalId": "CHANGE_TO_SHARED_EXTERNAL_ID"}}
  }]
}

Attach target-role permissions policy (read-only, all resources needed for inventory):
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {"Sid":"BackupRead","Effect":"Allow","Action":["backup:ListBackupVaults","backup:ListRecoveryPointsByBackupVault"],"Resource":"*"},
    {"Sid":"FileSystemsRead","Effect":"Allow","Action":["efs:DescribeFileSystems","fsx:DescribeFileSystems"],"Resource":"*"},
    {"Sid":"S3InventoryRead","Effect":"Allow","Action":["s3:ListAllMyBuckets","s3:GetBucketLocation"],"Resource":"*"},
    {"Sid":"CloudWatchMetricsRead","Effect":"Allow","Action":["cloudwatch:ListMetrics","cloudwatch:GetMetricStatistics"],"Resource":"*"}
  ]
}

NOTE: s3:GetBucketLocation for buckets restricted by bucket policies or SCPs may need special permission.
AWS Organizations is NOT required. Cross-account AssumeRole uses the listed account IDs.

2) MANAGEMENT ACCOUNT: Create execution role CentralStorageAuditLambdaRole.
Lambda service trust policy:
{
  "Version":"2012-10-17",
  "Statement":[{"Effect":"Allow","Principal":{"Service":"lambda.amazonaws.com"},"Action":"sts:AssumeRole"}]
}

Attach management-role permissions policy (replace account IDs, destination bucket, and prefix):
{
  "Version":"2012-10-17",
  "Statement":[
    {"Sid":"AssumeTargetRoles","Effect":"Allow","Action":"sts:AssumeRole","Resource":[
      "arn:aws:iam::111111111111:role/CentralStorageAuditReadRole",
      "arn:aws:iam::222222222222:role/CentralStorageAuditReadRole"
    ]},
    {"Sid":"WriteReport","Effect":"Allow","Action":"s3:PutObject","Resource":"arn:aws:s3:::MY_EXISTING_BUCKET/storage-audit/*"},
    {"Sid":"CreateLogs","Effect":"Allow","Action":"logs:CreateLogGroup","Resource":"arn:aws:logs:*:MANAGEMENT_ACCOUNT_ID:*"},
    {"Sid":"WriteLogs","Effect":"Allow","Action":["logs:CreateLogStream","logs:PutLogEvents"],"Resource":"arn:aws:logs:*:MANAGEMENT_ACCOUNT_ID:log-group:/aws/lambda/*:*"}
  ]
}

S3 bucket policy: Not required when bucket is in same management account and no explicit deny applies;
the Lambda role's identity policy can authorize PutObject. If cross-account bucket, its bucket policy
MUST explicitly authorize the Lambda execution-role principal s3:PutObject for the chosen prefix.

Optional SSE-KMS for REPORT bucket: Add to Lambda execution role:
{
 "Version":"2012-10-17",
 "Statement":[{"Effect":"Allow","Action":["kms:GenerateDataKey","kms:Decrypt"],
 "Resource":"arn:aws:kms:REGION:MANAGEMENT_ACCOUNT_ID:key/YOUR-KEY-ID"}]
}
The customer-managed KMS key policy must permit this role (directly or through IAM).
For S3 Bucket Keys or report reading, also grant kms:Decrypt to report readers as appropriate.
Reading EFS, FSx, AWS Backup, and CloudWatch metadata does NOT require decrypting their data keys.

3) LAMBDA SETTINGS (create directly in AWS Console; no SAM/CloudFormation)
Runtime: Python 3.12 or newer supported runtime with boto3.
Handler: lambda_function.lambda_handler
Architecture: x86_64 or arm64.
Timeout: up to 900 sec (15 min); start at 900 for many accounts/regions.
Memory: start 1024 MB; increase for large inventories and embedded HTML dataset.
Place the function outside a VPC unless VPC networking is necessary; VPC requires NAT or suitable endpoints.
Lambda must be able to reach AWS STS, S3, CloudWatch, Backup, EFS and FSx endpoints.

Environment variables example:
ACCOUNT_IDS=111111111111,222222222222
REGIONS=ap-southeast-2,ap-south-1,us-east-1
TARGET_ROLE_NAME=CentralStorageAuditReadRole
EXTERNAL_ID=CHANGE_TO_SHARED_EXTERNAL_ID
REPORT_BUCKET=MY_EXISTING_BUCKET
REPORT_PREFIX=storage-audit/production
MAX_WORKERS=4
# Optional, only for S3 SSE-KMS report encryption:
SSE_KMS_KEY_ID=arn:aws:kms:REGION:MANAGEMENT_ACCOUNT_ID:key/YOUR-KEY-ID

REGIONS must include every region you want scanned, and regions of S3 buckets you want reported.
The code reads ALL accounts given; include the management account as a target only if you create
and trust the target role there too.

4) DEPLOYMENT
- Create target IAM role with trust and read-only permissions in EACH target account.
- Create management Lambda execution role and attach management policy.
- AWS Lambda > Create function > Author from scratch > choose Python runtime and execution role.
- Paste/upload lambda_function.py and set handler as above.
- Set environment variables, timeout, memory, and click Deploy.
- Use a Test event: {} . The function returns the keys it uploaded.
- Read report from s3://MY_EXISTING_BUCKET/storage-audit/production/latest/storage-audit.html
  and dated report from s3://.../reports/storage-audit-YYYYMMDDTHHMMSSZ.html
- S3 console 'Open' or download HTML and open locally in browser; JavaScript filtering/export
  requires allowing local file JavaScript. For secure shared access, use an authenticated
  portal or controlled CloudFront distribution, not a public S3 bucket.
- Optionally schedule this Lambda with Amazon EventBridge Scheduler; allow lambda:InvokeFunction.
- Run once manually and review *-errors.json for partial failures before relying on totals.

5) LIMITATIONS AND COST ACCURACY
- AWS Backup: sizes = sum BackupSizeInBytes on recovery points, NOT actual physical/billable
  vault usage; incremental and shared storage prevents treating this as a billing total.
- S3: CloudWatch BucketSizeBytes daily metrics, including eligible storage-class overhead;
  blank/NO_METRIC means metric missing (NOT an empty bucket). Bucket total and class rows overlap.
- EFS: SizeInBytes metered Standard, IA and Archive; AWS updates periodically.
- FSx: ONTAP uses per-file-system StorageUsed SSD + StandardCapacityPool metrics; other FSx
  types show StorageUsed only IF published with the simple FileSystemId dimension.
  If unavailable, used size is blank; provisioned capacity remains visible. IA for
  non-ONTAP FSx types is not assumed. FSx provisioned capacity is GiB.
- Large accounts: Lambda 15-minute timeout / HTML memory can be exceeded. Split accounts into
  batches or regional invocations and merge results using Step Functions/S3 for very large estates.
- No delete, restore, modify, or S3 object-read permissions are requested.
